logs/spin-wheel-team-building#breadcrumbs\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"@type\": \"BreadcrumbList\",\n      \"@id\": \"https://spinthewheelsonline.com/blogs/spin-wheel-team-building#breadcrumbs\",\n      \"itemListElement\": [\n        {\n          \"@type\": \"ListItem\",\n          \"position\": 1,\n          \"name\": \"Home\",\n          \"item\": \"https://spinthewheelsonline.com/\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"@type\": \"ListItem\",\n          \"position\": 2,\n          \"name\": \"Blog\",\n          \"item\": \"https://spinthewheelsonline.com/blogs\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"@type\": \"ListItem\",\n          \"position\": 3,\n          \"name\": \"Spin Wheel Team Building\",\n          \"item\": \"https://spinthewheelsonline.com/blogs/spin-wheel-team-building\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"@type\": \"BlogPosting\",\n      \"@id\": \"https://spinthewheelsonline.com/blogs/spin-wheel-team-building#article\",\n      \"headline\": \"Spin the Wheel for Remote Teams: Decision Making & Collaboration\",\n      \"description\": \"How distributed teams use a free online spin wheel to make faster, fairer meeting decisions.\",\n      \"image\": \"https://spinthewheelsonline.com/eng-team-picker-wheel.webp\",\n      \"datePublished\": \"2026-10-15\",\n      \"dateModified\": \"2026-11-24\",\n      \"inLanguage\": \"en\",\n      \"author\": {\n        \"@id\": \"https://spinthewheelsonline.com/#harman\"\n      },\n      \"publisher\": {\n        \"@id\": \"https://spinthewheelsonline.com/#organization\"\n      },\n      \"mainEntityOfPage\": {\n        \"@id\": \"https://spinthewheelsonline.com/blogs/spin-wheel-team-building#webpage\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"@type\": \"FAQPage\",\n      \"@id\": \"https://spinthewheelsonline.com/blogs/spin-wheel-team-building#faq\",\n      \"mainEntity\": [\n        {\n          \"@type\": \"Question\",\n          \"name\": \"Can multiple people spin the same wheel at the same time?\",\n          \"acceptedAnswer\": {\n            \"@type\": \"Answer\",\n            \"text\": \"Each device runs its own instance of the wheel. For live team use, one person — usually the facilitator — screen-shares and spins. For async use, share the link with instructions on who spins.\"\n          }\n        },\n        {\n          \"@type\": \"Question\",\n          \"name\": \"Is it actually random, or can the person spinning influence the result?\",\n          \"acceptedAnswer\": {\n            \"@type\": \"Answer\",\n            \"text\": \"It is cryptographically random. The winning slice is drawn via the browser Web Cryptography API (window.crypto.getRandomValues) with rejection sampling before the visual animation starts, so click timing cannot steer the result.\"\n          }\n        },\n        {\n          \"@type\": \"Question\",\n          \"name\": \"Will it work during a Zoom, Teams, or Google Meet screen-share?\",\n          \"acceptedAnswer\": {\n            \"@type\": \"Answer\",\n            \"text\": \"Yes — it works on all major video conferencing platforms. Share your browser tab and, if you enable system audio, the ticking sound comes through too.\"\n          }\n        },\n        {\n          \"@type\": \"Question\",\n          \"name\": \"Is there a limit to how many team members I can add?\",\n          \"acceptedAnswer\": {\n            \"@type\": \"Answer\",\n            \"text\": \"Up to 500 entries fit cleanly per wheel—easily covering full departments or cross-functional teams.\"\n          }\n        }\n      ]\n    }\n  ]\n}"} />

