        <h2 id="faq">9. Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
        <div class="faq">
          <details class="faq-item">
            <summary>
              Can multiple people access and spin the same wheel at the same
              time?
            </summary>
            <div class="faq-a">
              <p>
                Each device runs its own instance. For live team use, one person
                — usually the facilitator — screen-shares and spins. For async
                use, share the link with instructions on who spins first.
                There's no real-time multiplayer sync, which is fine for most
                remote-team scenarios.
              </p>
            </div>
          </details>
          <details class="faq-item">
            <summary>
              Is it actually random, or can the person spinning influence the
              result?
            </summary>
            <div class="faq-a">
              <p>
                It is cryptographically random — the winning option is calculated via
                your browser's Web Cryptography API (<code>window.crypto.getRandomValues()</code>)
                with rejection sampling before the wheel animation begins, so click
                timing cannot steer the result. See
                <a href="/blogs/is-spin-wheel-truly-random" class="ilink"
                  >is a digital spin wheel truly random?</a
                >
                for the full explanation.
              </p>
            </div>
          </details>
          <details class="faq-item">
            <summary>
              Will it work during a Zoom, Teams, or Google Meet screen-share?
            </summary>
            <div class="faq-a">
              <p>
                Yes — it works on all major video conferencing platforms. Share
                your browser tab and, if you enable system audio sharing, the
                ticking sound comes through too.
              </p>
            </div>
          </details>
          <details class="faq-item">
            <summary>What if someone is absent from the meeting?</summary>
            <div class="faq-a">
              <p>
                Remove their entry before spinning. If a spin lands on someone
                who's absent, just spin again — the wheel has no memory of
                previous spins unless "remove after spin" is on, in which case
                their slot is already out of the pool for that session.
              </p>
            </div>
          </details>
          <details class="faq-item">
            <summary>
              What's the best way to use it for a fully async team?
            </summary>
            <div class="faq-a">
              <p>
                Share the wheel URL in your team channel with a clear
                instruction — "spin this to decide X, first click makes the
                call." Whoever spins can screenshot the result if you want a
                record. No extra process overhead.
              </p>
            </div>
          </details>
          <details class="faq-item">
            <summary>
              Is there a limit to how many team members I can add?
            </summary>
            <div class="faq-a">
              <p>
                Up to 500 entries load cleanly per wheel—more than enough for full squads, departments, or company all-hands rosters.
              </p>
            </div>
          </details>
        </div>

